#!/usr/bin/env node
// Pixel snapshots of the app's UI states, to prove a refactor changed no pixels.
//
//   scripts/agent/ui-snapshots capture <Debug app> <out dir> [--only a,b] [--js host:port] [--keep]
//   scripts/agent/ui-snapshots compare <before dir> <after dir> [--tolerance N]
//   scripts/agent/ui-snapshots list
//   scripts/agent/ui-snapshots -h | --help
//
// capture launches a hidden, onboarded instance (scripts/lib/instance.mjs) on a fixed seeded session: two profiles,
// pinned tabs, a tab group, tabs on local file pages, bookmarks, history on fixed past dates, finished downloads.
// Search suggestions and telemetry are off and Chrome sits behind a dead proxy, so nothing reaches the network; it
// waits for uBlock Origin's bundled lists. Its data dir is always ~/ardia-scratch/ui-snapshots/data (the path
// shows in Settings), so captures take turns on a lock. Each state is driven through the dev harness and written
// as <out dir>/<state>.png with ac.shell.devSnapshotWindow (in-process, transparent background, works with the
// screen locked) once consecutive snapshots are byte-identical. <out dir>/states.json has each state's result and
// <out dir>/manifest.json the app, the JS source and the checkout's commit. --only captures just those states;
// --js takes the JS from another Metro (default: this checkout's on :8081, pinned); --keep leaves the instance up.
//
// compare diffs every PNG present in either dir: per state the count of differing pixels and the largest channel
// delta, a <after dir>/diff/<state>.png for each state that differs (changed pixels red over a dimmed copy), and
// exits 1 when any state differs by more than --tolerance pixels (default 0: two captures of one build are
// byte-identical), is missing on one side, or failed to capture.
